NAME
       head - output the first part of files

SYNOPSIS
       head [-n N] [-c N] [-qv] [FILE]...

DESCRIPTION
       Print the first 10 lines of each FILE. With more than one FILE, precede
       each with a header.

OPTIONS
       -n N, -N
           print the first N lines; with a negative N, all but the last N lines

       -c N
           print the first N bytes

       -q
           never print headers

       -v
           always print headers

EXAMPLES
       head -n 3 /etc/passwd
       ls /bin | head

SEE ALSO
       tail(1), cat(1)
